# CHRONOS — Model tier policy (hard constraint)

The full policy lives in `context/game logic context/roadmap.md` under **MODEL TIER POLICY**. Treat it as binding for every **LLM / embedding** integration, not a preference.

## All-Gemini runtime (migration 2026-04-23)

**All LLM calls → Google Gemini (`CHRONOS_GEMINI_MODEL`, default `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`).**

The historic fast/quality tier split has been retired. Ollama is no longer used.
The `tier` parameter on `call_llm` is accepted for backward compat but is a no-op.

Call sites (all now route to Gemini):
- `action_parser` — NL → structured action, strict JSON
- `autonomous_action_light` — 1-sentence offscreen NPC activity
- `autonomous_action` — full NPC autonomous actions
- `death_check` — short structured JSON
- `region_knowledge` — one-line map-click note
- `npc_perception` — one-line NPC hover note
- `historical_context` — 2-3 sentence passage explainer
- `memory_fade` — one-sentence fade framing
- `npc_pov` — NPC reactions to player actions
- `character_gen` — player + NPCs at run start (8-15 concurrent, rate-limited via semaphore)
- `ground_context` — HCE run-start + refresh
- `erasure` — the final narrative passage when the run ends (fires exactly once)

**NoOp fallback.** When Gemini is unavailable:
- `GEMINI_API_KEY` is unset → ERROR log; all calls return `("...", cost=$0)`
- the Gemini circuit breaker is open (3 failures in 60s → 5 minutes open) → WARNING log
- a single Gemini call raises after retries → WARNING log; circuit records the failure

The NoOp response keeps turns alive on transient failures. The player sees degraded prose ("...") rather than a 500 error. Circuit breaker prevents cascading failures.

## Per-run cost ceiling

- **~€0.022 median per 10-turn run** (gemini-2.5-flash-lite at $0.10/$0.40 per M in/out)
- **€1.00 soft cap** — UI banner, dismissible, once per run; turns continue
- **€2.00 hard cap** — ALL turn-advancing endpoints reject further advances with `402` + `code: cost_cap_hard`; applies to `/turn`, `/skip`, AND `/turn` with `dead_observing` status (observation mode still burns tokens); player can still read the world and end the run manually via `DELETE /api/run/{id}`

Internal accounting is USD (Gemini bills USD). EUR conversion happens at render time via `config.USD_TO_EUR`. The cap *values* are in EUR — forex drift shifts the real cap silently; see the TODO on `USD_TO_EUR` in `backend/config.py`.

## Before writing any LLM call

1. **All calls go to Gemini.** The `tier` parameter is a deprecated no-op — don't add new `tier` routing logic.
2. **New call sites:** adding a new `call_llm` call is a design decision. Flag it for user review before merge. Estimate its per-run cost contribution.
3. **Use `call_site="..."`.** This is how `track_turn_cost()` warnings identify uncovered endpoints.

## Concurrency

`GEMINI_MAX_CONCURRENT_CEILING = 20` (hard constant, cannot be exceeded by env var).
`CHRONOS_GEMINI_MAX_CONCURRENT` default is `15`. Paid tier (300 RPM) absorbs this comfortably.

## Embeddings

`nomic-embed-text` (local), if/when embeddings are used.

## Cost and architecture

If a change would push per-run cost above the **€1.00 soft cap** or **€2.00 hard cap**, **surface it** — the architecture is wrong for project policy. The all-Gemini migration target is ~€0.022 median per 10-turn run, well below the €0.31 roadmap target.
